@
_tmp*
state/*.jpg
state/*.mp4
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# rendered videos and scratch space never belong in git (each channel has
# its own pair of folders, so ignore both generations)
factory/out/
factory/out_*/
factory/work/
factory/work_*/
yt_auth/*token.pickle
yt_auth/*client_secrets.json
yt_auth/*.json
# the chess queue past ~5 years stays in the local archive; the runner
# keeps the first 1999 episodes in git - decades of daily runway at
# one episode a day, and the checkout stays seconds instead of minutes
factory/content_chess/chess_part[2-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*
factory/content_chess/chess_part1[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*
# regenerable data blobs - never in git (the wiki cache alone is
# 70 MB of crawl output and it single-handedly killed every push)
wiki_cache/
puzzles_db.zst
puzzles_pool_big.jsonl
topics_sci_old_generic.txt

# local chess backups never belong in git
factory/content_chess_backup_*/

# webads project scratch: rendered reels and thumb tests are artifacts,
# not source (the 10k bank itself IS committed as one jsonl)
projects/webads/_work/
projects/webads/out/

# multichan brand art (200 jpgs, 19 MB) ships to the public brands repo,
# never to this one - the banner URLs in set_brand.py point at raw GitHub
projects/multichan/brands/
